The [[Hungry Blade]] is an epic [[Vampiric]] [[melee]] [[weapon]] available in the shop for all classes. With no synergy, its damage is mild, but its max damage is increased by the amount of {{icon/vampirism}} the character has, and can become extremely high in the right build. It can be greatly improved by ensuring there is a source of {{icon/regeneration}}, since this will cause the [[Hungry Blade]] to grow the character's {{icon/vampirism}}.

There are a number of interesting [[Hungry Blade]] "upgrades", although some of them have very different properties. 

[[Hungry Blade]] and [[Thorn Whip]] combine into the powerful [[Bloodthorne]], which scales off of both {{icon/vampirism}} and {{icon/spikes}}, and can gain both by using {{icon/regeneration}}. It's much harder-hitting and slightly more stamina-consuming than the [[Hungry Blade]], much smaller than the [[Thorn Whip]], and generally speaking, better than either one.

[[Hungry Blade]] and [[Mana Orb]] combine into the [[Manathirst]], which is mainly good for generating {{icon/mana}} on-hit and delivering a {{icon/vampirism}}-scaling hit once a high enough amount of {{icon/mana}} is gained. The [[Manathirst]] and [[Hungry Blade]] don't necessarily thrive in the same builds, and it shouldn't be considered a generic upgrade. 

[[Hungry Blade]] and [[Snowball]] combine into the [[Frostbite]], which is the [[ice]]-themed variant. The [[Frostbite]] scales off of both {{icon/vampirism}} and {{icon/cold}}, and inflicts {{icon/cold}} on hit. Once a high {{icon/cold}} threshold is reached, it will also give a one-time burst of {{icon/vampirism}}. The [[Frostbite]] is arguably less good at generating {{icon/vampirism}} than the [[Hungry Blade]], but in a [[Vampirism]] build with other ways to generate {{icon/vampirism}}, the [[Frostbite]] is still likely better, since it gains +1 damage per {{icon/vampirism}}, rather than +1 maximum damage, and gains even more damage from the {{icon/cold}} generated.

Most of these upgrades (not the [[Manathirst]]) also have one more socket than the [[Hungry Blade]].

